---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Cosmic Strings Cheat Sheet | Free Topological Defects, Gravitational Waves"
  description="Complete cosmic strings cheat sheet with topological defects and gravitational waves. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Cosmic Strings<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Topological defects and gravitational waves. From symmetry breaking to observational signatures.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Theory</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Formation</h3>
        <pre><code>Symmetry breaking in early universe
Phase transitions at T ~ 10¹⁶ GeV
Topological defects: 1D strings
Energy density: μ ~ (η/c²)²
η: symmetry breaking scale</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Tension: μ ~ 10²² kg/m (GUT scale)
Length: could be horizon-sized
Move at relativistic speeds
Intercommute: strings can reconnect
Network evolution: scaling solution</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Gravitational Effects</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Gravitational Waves</h3>
        <pre><code>Cusps: loops emit GW bursts
Kinks: sharp bends emit GW
Stochastic background from string network
LISA: sensitive to Gμ ~ 10⁻¹⁷-10⁻¹¹
Pulsar timing: sensitive to Gμ ~ 10⁻¹¹-10⁻⁷</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Observational Signatures</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Detection Methods</h3>
        <pre><code>CMB: Kaiser-Stebbins effect (line discontinuity)
Gravitational lensing: double images
21 cm: absorption features
Gravitational waves: bursts and background
Large-scale structure: filament formation</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Constraints</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Current Limits</h3>
        <pre><code>Gμ < 10⁻⁷ (pulsar timing)
Gμ < 10⁻¹¹ (CMB)
Gμ < 10⁻⁷ (gravitational lensing)
GUT strings: Gμ ~ 10⁻⁶ (partially ruled out)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
